# `out*/`, not `out-*/`: the default --prefix in CI and in the docs is a BARE `out/`, which the
# narrower pattern missed. A local build then leaves ~1200 files of installed ExecuTorch sitting
# untracked-but-not-ignored, where a `git add -A` sweeps them into a commit.
out*/
# The gate's ccache directory (full-aot job); must never be committed.
.ccache/
et-build/
spike/*.log
et-build-*/
etnp-extras-*/
.superpowers/
dist/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# Python virtual environments. A bare `venv/` was committed once already (1945 files, ~99MB in
# 1c2669f) by exactly the `git add -A` sweep described at the top of this file, and a checked-in
# venv is dead weight either way: it bakes absolute interpreter paths, so it is unusable on any
# other machine. Cover the common names rather than the one that bit us -- `*-venv/` catches the
# `.export-venv/` that extras/README.md tells you to create right here in the repo.
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/
*-venv/
*.venv/
